# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide builds a circuit for the **time dynamics of the one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard model**, from writing down the Hamiltonian to checking the evolved site densities. What makes the route interesting is a single idea, taken from the *flow set* framework of Gandon et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), the work that also motivated the [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") in this package:\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa ang gabay na ito ng circuit para sa **time dynamics ng one-dimensional na Fermi-Hubbard model**, mula sa pagsulat ng Hamiltonian hanggang sa pagsuri ng mga evolved na site density. Ang nagpapainteresante sa ruta ay isang ideya, mula sa *flow set* framework nina Gandon et al. <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), ang gawang nagbigay-inspirasyon din sa [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") sa package na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Instead of grouping Hamiltonian terms *after* the fermion-to-qubit mapping, group them *before* it, into **flow sets**, one-dimensional subsets of the directed fermionic interaction graph whose transfer operators mutually commute.\n"
msgstr "> Sa halip na i-group ang mga term ng Hamiltonian *pagkatapos* ng fermion-to-qubit mapping, i-group ang mga ito *bago* ito, tungo sa **flow sets**, mga one-dimensional na subset ng directed fermionic interaction graph na ang mga transfer operator ay sabay-sabay na nagko-commute.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That choice drives everything below. It calls for the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpiling iyon ang nagtutulak sa lahat ng nasa ibaba. Nangangailangan ito ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **custom fermion-to-qubit encoding** tailored to the flow sets, which here spends one **ancilla qubit** so the qubit count associated with the implementation of a given Hamiltonian term no longer grows with the number of fermionic modes (as is the case for Jordan-Wigner (JW)).\n"
msgstr "Isang **custom na fermion-to-qubit encoding** na iniakma sa mga flow set, na dito ay gumagamit ng isang **ancilla qubit** para hindi na lumaki ang bilang ng qubit na kaugnay ng pagpapatupad ng isang Hamiltonian term kasabay ng bilang ng mga fermionic mode (tulad ng nangyayari sa Jordan-Wigner (JW)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **custom synthesis** that exploits the commutativity within each set. The payoff is a circuit whose two-qubit depth is **constant in the system size**, against the linear growth of a JW-based term-by-term Trotterization.\n"
msgstr "Isang **custom na synthesis** na sinasamantala ang commutativity sa loob ng bawat set. Ang kapalit nito ay isang circuit na ang two-qubit depth ay **pare-pareho sa laki ng system**, kumpara sa linear na paglaki ng term-by-term na Trotterization na nakabatay sa JW.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The machinery that gets an encoding of your own into the transpiler ([`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\")) carries over to any model.\n"
msgstr "Ang makinaryang nagpapasok ng sarili mong encoding sa transpiler ([`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") at [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\")) ay naaangkop sa kahit anong model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the transpiler stages referenced throughout, and the [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) for the general recipe for writing a custom mapper.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tingnan din\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) para sa mga transpiler stage na tinutukoy sa buong gabay, at ang [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) para sa pangkalahatang recipe sa pagsulat ng custom na mapper.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transfer operators and flow sets {#transfer-operators-and-flow-sets}"
msgstr "Mga transfer operator at flow set {#transfer-operators-and-flow-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") is built from vertex operators $V_j$ and transfer operators $T_{jk}$. In terms of fermionic creation and annihilation operators,\n"
msgstr "Ang isang [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") ay binubuo mula sa mga vertex operator na $V_j$ at mga transfer operator na $T_{jk}$. Sa mga termino ng fermionic creation at annihilation operator,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = 1 - 2 a^\\dagger_j a_j \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\left( a^\\dagger_j - a_j \\right)\n"
"                       \\left( a^\\dagger_k + a_k \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = 1 - 2 a^\\dagger_j a_j \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\left( a^\\dagger_j - a_j \\right)\n"
"                       \\left( a^\\dagger_k + a_k \\right) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so $V_j$ measures the occupation of mode $j$ (it is $+1$ when empty and $-1$ when filled), while $T_{jk}$ transfers a fermion along the *directed* edge $j \\to k$. Note that the two indices of $T_{jk}$ are *not* interchangeable. The first index carries the minus combination and the second carries the plus, which is what makes $T_{jk}$ distinct from $T_{kj}$ and gives the edge its orientation.\n"
msgstr "kaya sinusukat ng $V_j$ ang occupation ng mode na $j$ (ito ay $+1$ kapag walang laman at $-1$ kapag puno), samantalang inililipat ng $T_{jk}$ ang isang fermion sa *directed* na edge na $j \\to k$. Tandaan na ang dalawang index ng $T_{jk}$ ay *hindi* mapagpapalit. Dala ng unang index ang minus na kombinasyon at dala ng pangalawa ang plus, kaya naiiba ang $T_{jk}$ sa $T_{kj}$ at nagkakaroon ng oryentasyon ang edge.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These satisfy *mixed* commutation relations. Two transfer operators acting on **disjoint** sites commute trivially, since each is an *even* product of fermionic operators. The interesting case is a shared site. There, the two **commute** if the arrows *flow* through that site (one arrives, one leaves) and **anticommute** if they *clash* (both arrive, or both leave).\n"
msgstr "Ang mga ito ay sumusunod sa *halo-halong* commutation relation. Ang dalawang transfer operator na umaaksyon sa **magkahiwalay** na site ay nagko-commute nang trivial, dahil ang bawat isa ay isang *even* na product ng mga fermionic operator. Ang kawili-wiling kaso ay ang nakabahaging site. Doon, ang dalawa ay **nagko-commute** kung ang mga arrow ay *dumadaloy* sa site na iyon (isa ang dumarating, isa ang umaalis) at **nag-aanticommute** kung *nagbabanggaan* ang mga ito (parehong dumarating, o parehong umaalis).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rule is easiest to see on a picture. Drawing the vertices as nodes and each $T_{jk}$ as an arrow from $j$ to $k$ gives the *directed* interaction graph, here for the four-site chain used throughout this guide, which carries both orientations of every bond:\n"
msgstr "Pinakamadaling makita ang patakaran sa isang larawan. Kapag iginuhit ang mga vertex bilang mga node at ang bawat $T_{jk}$ bilang arrow mula $j$ patungong $k$, makukuha ang *directed* na interaction graph, na narito para sa four-site chain na ginagamit sa buong gabay na ito, na may parehong oryentasyon ng bawat bond:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A four-site chain with both orientations of every bond drawn as arrows.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A four-site chain with both orientations of every bond drawn as arrows.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace the rule on the figure. Look at $T_{1,2}$ and $T_{2,3}$, for example. One arrow *arrives* at site 2 and the other *leaves* it, so the fermion flows straight through and the two operators commute. Look instead at $T_{1,2}$ and $T_{3,2}$. Both arrows *point into* site 2. They clash, and those two anticommute.\n"
msgstr "Sundan ang patakaran sa figure. Tingnan halimbawa ang $T_{1,2}$ at $T_{2,3}$. Isang arrow ang *dumarating* sa site 2 at ang isa ay *umaalis* dito, kaya diretsong dumadaloy ang fermion at nagko-commute ang dalawang operator. Tingnan naman ang $T_{1,2}$ at $T_{3,2}$. Parehong *tumuturo papasok* sa site 2 ang dalawang arrow. Nagbabanggaan sila, at nag-aanticommute ang dalawang iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is what makes flow sets possible. Pick a set of arrows forming a directed path and every pair either meets head-to-tail or does not meet at all, so the whole set commutes, even though the individual operators overlap on shared sites. Evolving under a single flow set therefore incurs **no Trotter error**, and as [step 7](#flowsets-synthesis) shows, it can also be done at constant circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang nagpapagana sa mga flow set. Pumili ng set ng mga arrow na bumubuo ng directed path at ang bawat pares ay alinman sa nagtatagpo nang head-to-tail o hindi nagtatagpo, kaya nagko-commute ang buong set, kahit nagsasapaw ang mga indibidwal na operator sa mga nakabahaging site. Kaya ang pag-evolve sa ilalim ng iisang flow set ay may **walang Trotter error**, at tulad ng ipinapakita ng [step 7](#flowsets-synthesis), magagawa rin ito sa constant na circuit depth.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian {#1-the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1. Ang Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian {#1-the-fermi-hubbard-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 1D Fermi-Hubbard model on $L$ sites (spinless, open boundaries) is\n"
msgstr "Ang 1D Fermi-Hubbard model sa $L$ na site (spinless, open boundaries) ay\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j} \\left( a^\\dagger_j a_{j+1} + a^\\dagger_{j+1} a_j \\right)\n"
"    + U \\sum_{j} n_j n_{j+1} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j} \\left( a^\\dagger_j a_{j+1} + a^\\dagger_{j+1} a_j \\right)\n"
"    + U \\sum_{j} n_j n_{j+1} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Following Eq. (9) of Ref. <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), the hopping term is $t \\sum_j (T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$. The interaction is diagonal, so it is expressed through vertex operators using $n_j = (1 - V_j)/2$:\n"
msgstr "Ayon sa Eq. (9) ng Ref. <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), ang hopping term ay $t \\sum_j (T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$. Diagonal ang interaction, kaya ipinapahayag ito sa pamamagitan ng mga vertex operator gamit ang $n_j = (1 - V_j)/2$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"n_j n_{j+1} = \\tfrac{1}{4}\\left( 1 - V_j - V_{j+1} + V_j V_{j+1} \\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"n_j n_{j+1} = \\tfrac{1}{4}\\left( 1 - V_j - V_{j+1} + V_j V_{j+1} \\right) \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both pieces are built directly as a [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Note that $V_j$ is stored as the diagonal entry `(j, j)`:\n"
msgstr "Ang dalawang bahagi ay direktang binuo bilang isang [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Tandaan na ang $V_j$ ay iniimbak bilang diagonal na entry na `(j, j)`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interior sites pick up a coefficient of $-1$ on $V_j$ because they appear in two bonds, whereas the boundary sites only appear in one. Every term listed here appears in the graph drawn above. The `T(j,k)` terms are its arrows, and the `V(j)` terms its nodes.\n"
msgstr "Nagkakaroon ang mga interior site ng coefficient na $-1$ sa $V_j$ dahil lumilitaw sila sa dalawang bond, samantalang ang mga boundary site ay lumilitaw lamang sa isa. Ang bawat term na nakalista rito ay lumilitaw sa graph na iginuhit sa itaas. Ang mga term na `T(j,k)` ay ang mga arrow nito, at ang mga term na `V(j)` ay ang mga node nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"partition-into-flow-sets\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Partition into flow sets {#2-partition-into-flow-sets}"
msgstr "2. I-partition sa mga flow set {#2-partition-into-flow-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, label each term with the flow set it belongs to. The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") attribute exists for this purpose. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over a grouped operator decomposes into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") per group ([step 6](#flowsets-transpile) puts this to work), so the grouping decided here at the *fermionic* level survives into the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, lagyan ng label ang bawat term ng flow set na kinabibilangan nito. Para dito ang attribute na [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\"). Ang isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate sa isang grouped na operator ay nagde-decompose sa isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") bawat group ([ginagamit ito ng step 6](#flowsets-transpile)), kaya ang pag-group na napagpasyahan dito sa *fermionic* na antas ay nananatili hanggang sa circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the 1D chain, the two hopping flow sets are the east-oriented arrows ($T_{j,j+1}$) and the west-oriented arrows ($T_{j+1,j}$). The diagonal interaction terms commute with everything diagonal and form a third group:\n"
msgstr "Para sa 1D chain, ang dalawang hopping flow set ay ang mga arrow na nakaharap sa silangan ($T_{j,j+1}$) at ang mga arrow na nakaharap sa kanluran ($T_{j+1,j}$). Ang mga diagonal na interaction term ay nagko-commute sa lahat ng diagonal at bumubuo ng ikatlong group:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups 0 and 1 are the two flow sets. Each set is a directed path along the chain, so by the flow property all terms within a group commute.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga group 0 at 1 ang dalawang flow set. Ang bawat set ay isang directed path sa kahabaan ng chain, kaya ayon sa flow property, nagko-commute ang lahat ng term sa loob ng isang group.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group also has to be Hermitian on its own, since a product formula exponentiates the groups separately and only a Hermitian factor has a unitary evolution. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") confirms it:\n"
msgstr "Dapat ding Hermitian ang bawat group sa sarili nito, dahil ine-exponentiate nang hiwalay ng product formula ang mga group at tanging Hermitian na factor lang ang may unitary na evolution. Kinukumpirma ito ng [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is worth pausing on, because the two hopping groups are *one-directional*: group 0 holds only east-oriented terms and group 1 only west-oriented ones. Splitting a Hamiltonian that way would normally break Hermiticity, since $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ needs its conjugate partner $a^\\dagger_k a_j$ alongside it. A [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") avoids the problem because $T_{jk}$ is *already* Hermitian on its own. It is a product of two Majorana operators (see its definition in step 1), not a bare $a^\\dagger_j a_k$, so its Jordan-Wigner image carries a real coefficient rather than an imaginary one. Choosing this operator representation is therefore what makes a one-directional flow set a legitimate Trotter factor at all.\n"
msgstr "Sulit itong pagtuunan ng pansin, dahil ang dalawang hopping group ay *one-directional*: ang group 0 ay may hawak lamang na mga term na nakaharap sa silangan at ang group 1 ay lamang sa kanluran. Karaniwang sisira sa Hermiticity ang paghahati ng Hamiltonian sa ganoong paraan, dahil kailangan ng $a^\\dagger_j a_k$ ang conjugate partner nitong $a^\\dagger_k a_j$ kasama nito. Naiiwasan ito ng [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") dahil ang $T_{jk}$ ay *Hermitian na* sa sarili nito. Isa itong product ng dalawang Majorana operator (tingnan ang kahulugan nito sa step 1), hindi isang hubad na $a^\\dagger_j a_k$, kaya ang Jordan-Wigner image nito ay may real na coefficient sa halip na imaginary. Kaya ang pagpili sa operator representation na ito ang nagpapahintulot na maging lehitimong Trotter factor ang one-directional na flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The east/west labels used throughout this guide are **geometric**, with the chain drawn left to right and mode indices increasing in that direction; $T_{j,j+1}$ points east and $T_{j+1,j}$ points west. Ref.   <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) is internally inconsistent on this naming (its prose and its figures disagree) so this guide deliberately does *not* follow the prose, and instead keeps the labels from the picture. When cross-reading with the paper, match the flow sets by their Pauli weights (1 and 3 below), not by the compass words.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang mga label na east/west na ginagamit sa buong gabay na ito ay **geometric**, na ang chain ay iginuhit mula kaliwa pakanan at tumataas ang mga mode index sa direksyong iyon; ang $T_{j,j+1}$ ay nakaturo sa silangan at ang $T_{j+1,j}$ ay nakaturo sa kanluran. Ang Ref.   <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) ay hindi pare-pareho sa pagpapangalang ito (hindi magkatugma ang prosa at mga figure nito) kaya sadyang *hindi* sinusunod ng gabay na ito ang prosa, at sa halip ay pinananatili ang mga label mula sa larawan. Kapag binabasa kasabay ng paper, itugma ang mga flow set ayon sa kanilang Pauli weight (1 at 3 sa ibaba), hindi ayon sa mga salitang compass.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"write-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Write the custom encoding {#3-write-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "3. Isulat ang custom na encoding {#3-write-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Section IV B of Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) classifies the forms that a local fermion-to-qubit encoding can take when restricted to a flow set. Plain Jordan-Wigner uses $N_q = N_f$ qubits and maps every hopping term to a weight-2 Pauli. The classification shows that **spending extra qubits buys structure** in the encoded operators.\n"
msgstr "Inuuri ng Seksyon IV B ng Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) ang mga anyong maaaring taglayin ng isang lokal na fermion-to-qubit encoding kapag nakalimita sa isang flow set. Gumagamit ang simpleng Jordan-Wigner ng $N_q = N_f$ na qubit at nima-map ang bawat hopping term sa isang weight-2 na Pauli. Ipinapakita ng klasipikasyon na **ang paggastos ng dagdag na qubit ay bumibili ng istruktura** sa mga na-encode na operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding implemented here is the parity-delocalized construction of Appendix B 2 (equations B4 and B5), which uses one **ancilla qubit**, so $N_q = N_f + 1$. The fermionic parity is delocalized across a pair of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Ang encoding na ipinatupad dito ay ang parity-delocalized na konstruksyon ng Appendix B 2 (mga equation B4 at B5), na gumagamit ng isang **ancilla qubit**, kaya $N_q = N_f + 1$. Ang fermionic parity ay dine-delocalize sa isang pares ng qubit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j,j+1} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} X_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j+1,j} = +\\tfrac{1}{2} Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j,j+1} = -\\tfrac{1}{2} X_{j+1} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{j+1,j} = +\\tfrac{1}{2} Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The index $j+2$ in the last expression forces the extra qubit. The chain’s final bond has $j = N_f - 2$, so its $Z_{j+2}$ lands on qubit $N_f$, one past the last fermionic mode $N_f - 1$. That trailing qubit is the ancilla, and it is why $N_q = N_f + 1$ rather than $N_f$. The same reach shows up in $V_j$, whose $Z_{j+1}$ is on the ancilla for $j = N_f - 1$.\n"
msgstr "Ang index na $j+2$ sa huling expression ang nagpapatawag ng dagdag na qubit. Ang huling bond ng chain ay may $j = N_f - 2$, kaya ang $Z_{j+2}$ nito ay napupunta sa qubit $N_f$, isa pagkatapos ng huling fermionic mode na $N_f - 1$. Ang nasa hulihang qubit na iyon ang ancilla, at iyon ang dahilan kung bakit $N_q = N_f + 1$ at hindi $N_f$. Makikita rin ang parehong abot sa $V_j$, na ang $Z_{j+1}$ ay nasa ancilla para sa $j = N_f - 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff is visible immediately; one whole flow set is mapped to a sum of weight-1 Paulis.\n"
msgstr "Agad na kita ang kapalit; ang isang buong flow set ay nima-map sa isang sum ng mga weight-1 na Pauli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ prefactors are fixed by the normalization $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac{1}{4}$, and the relative minus sign between the two orientations is fixed by the product identity $T_{j,j+1} = -V_j V_{j+1} T_{j+1,j}$, which the Paulis above satisfy. Getting either wrong yields an operator that obeys the commutation relations but no longer represents the same Hamiltonian, so you should verify the encoding numerically, as shown in [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang mga prefactor na $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ ay itinakda ng normalization na $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac{1}{4}$, at ang relatibong minus sign sa pagitan ng dalawang oryentasyon ay itinakda ng product identity na $T_{j,j+1} = -V_j V_{j+1} T_{j+1,j}$, na sinasang-ayunan ng mga Pauli sa itaas. Ang pagkakamali sa alinman ay magbibigay ng operator na sumusunod sa mga commutation relation pero hindi na kumakatawan sa parehong Hamiltonian, kaya dapat mong i-verify ang encoding nang numerikal, tulad ng ipinapakita sa [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing the encoding means writing a function that maps a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") handles the iteration over terms and their composition:\n"
msgstr "Ang pagsulat ng encoding ay nangangahulugan ng pagsulat ng function na nima-map ang isang generalized transfer operator sa isang Pauli string; hinahawakan ng [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") ang pag-iterate sa mga term at ang pagbubuo ng mga ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn\") expects the signature `(operator, num_qubits)`, and the return type must be a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), which makes the function directly usable as a transpiler plugin. See [step 6](#flowsets-transpile).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Mahalaga\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Inaasahan ng [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.mapper_fn\") ang signature na `(operator, num_qubits)`, at ang return type ay dapat isang [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), na nagpapagamit sa function nang direkta bilang transpiler plugin. Tingnan ang [step 6](#flowsets-transpile).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying it to the Hamiltonian from step 1 gives the encoded operator on $N_f + 1 = 5$ qubits:\n"
msgstr "Ang paglalapat nito sa Hamiltonian mula sa step 1 ay nagbibigay ng na-encode na operator sa $N_f + 1 = 5$ na qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are 14 terms, in three shapes: the hopping has become `X` and `ZXZ`, the interaction `ZZ`, and the leading `[]` is the identity, contributing only a global phase. Note that the `ZZ` terms reach nearest *and* next-nearest neighbors; $V_jV_{j+1}$ spans qubits $j$ through $j+2$, which is the cost of delocalizing the parity.\n"
msgstr "Mayroong 14 na term, sa tatlong hugis: ang hopping ay naging `X` at `ZXZ`, ang interaction ay `ZZ`, at ang nangunguna na `[]` ay ang identity, na nag-aambag lamang ng global phase. Tandaan na ang mga term na `ZZ` ay umaabot sa pinakamalapit *at* susunod na pinakamalapit na kapitbahay; ang $V_jV_{j+1}$ ay sumasaklaw sa mga qubit na $j$ hanggang $j+2$, na siyang gastos ng pag-delocalize ng parity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grouping by flow set exposes the asymmetry the construction buys. List the Pauli weights present in each group:\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-group ayon sa flow set ang naglalantad ng asymmetry na binibili ng konstruksyon. Ilista ang mga Pauli weight na naroon sa bawat group:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The east-oriented flow set (group 0) consists **entirely of weight-1 Paulis**. Its time evolution is therefore a layer of single-qubit rotations and needs *no entangling gates*, whereas under Jordan-Wigner every hopping term is weight-2 and requires them. This is the space-time trade-off of Ref. <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) in its simplest form: one extra qubit converts half of the hopping Hamiltonian into single-qubit rotations.\n"
msgstr "Ang flow set na nakaharap sa silangan (group 0) ay binubuo **nang buo ng weight-1 na Pauli**. Kaya ang time evolution nito ay isang layer ng single-qubit rotation at *hindi nangangailangan ng entangling gate*, samantalang sa Jordan-Wigner ang bawat hopping term ay weight-2 at nangangailangan ng mga ito. Ito ang space-time trade-off ng Ref. <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) sa pinakasimpleng anyo nito: ang isang dagdag na qubit ay nagko-convert sa kalahati ng hopping Hamiltonian tungo sa mga single-qubit rotation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The west-oriented flow set (group 1) pays for it at weight three, and the interaction (group 2) sits at weight two, where the weight-zero entry is the identity. None of this is yet a *circuit* claim; what a synthesis makes of these weights is the subject of steps 6 and 7.\n"
msgstr "Ang flow set na nakaharap sa kanluran (group 1) ay nagbabayad para dito sa weight tatlo, at ang interaction (group 2) ay nasa weight dalawa, kung saan ang weight-zero na entry ay ang identity. Wala pa sa mga ito ang claim tungkol sa *circuit*; ang magagawa ng isang synthesis sa mga weight na ito ang paksa ng mga step 6 at 7.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Verify the encoding {#4-verify-the-encoding}"
msgstr "4. I-verify ang encoding {#4-verify-the-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A custom encoding is only useful if it is *faithful*, and a hand-written one should be checked. Because this encoding uses $N_f + 1$ qubits, the qubit Hilbert space is twice as large as the fermionic one, so the encoded Hamiltonian cannot equal the Jordan-Wigner one term by term. The two are related by an isometry instead.\n"
msgstr "Kapaki-pakinabang lamang ang custom na encoding kung ito ay *tapat*, at dapat suriin ang isinulat nang mano-mano. Dahil gumagamit ang encoding na ito ng $N_f + 1$ na qubit, dalawang beses na mas malaki ang qubit Hilbert space kaysa sa fermionic, kaya hindi maaaring maging katumbas ng Jordan-Wigner ang na-encode na Hamiltonian term por term. Sa halip, magkaugnay ang dalawa sa pamamagitan ng isang isometry.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Where the isometry comes from:** Under Jordan-Wigner a basis state is the occupation string; qubit $j$ holds $n_j$. This encoding instead stores *cumulative parities*. Define\n"
msgstr "**Pinagmulan ng isometry:** Sa ilalim ng Jordan-Wigner, ang basis state ay ang occupation string; hawak ng qubit $j$ ang $n_j$. Sa halip, iniimbak ng encoding na ito ang *cumulative parities*. Tukuyin ang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b_0 = 0 \\, , \\qquad b_{j+1} = n_0 \\oplus n_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus n_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b_0 = 0 \\, , \\qquad b_{j+1} = n_0 \\oplus n_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus n_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so bit $b_{j+1}$ records the parity of all occupations up to and including site $j$. There are $N_f + 1$ such bits for $N_f$ occupations, which is where the ancilla comes from. The occupation is recovered as the *difference* between neighboring bits, $n_j = b_j \\oplus b_{j+1}$. An occupied site therefore shows up as a **domain wall** between two adjacent bits, which is why this is called a domain-wall (or Kramers-Wannier) encoding. That is also why $V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1}$: the product of two neighboring $Z$s reads off that difference.\n"
msgstr "kaya itinatala ng bit na $b_{j+1}$ ang parity ng lahat ng occupation hanggang at kasama ang site $j$. Mayroong $N_f + 1$ na ganoong bit para sa $N_f$ na occupation, na pinagmumulan ng ancilla. Nababawi ang occupation bilang *pagkakaiba* ng magkalapit na bit, $n_j = b_j \\oplus b_{j+1}$. Kaya ang isang occupied na site ay lumilitaw bilang **domain wall** sa pagitan ng dalawang magkatabing bit, kaya ito tinatawag na domain-wall (o Kramers-Wannier) encoding. Iyon din ang dahilan kung bakit $V_j = Z_j Z_{j+1}$: binabasa ng product ng dalawang magkalapit na $Z$ ang pagkakaibang iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing this map out for a few states makes the structure concrete (note that $b_0 = 0$ is fixed, so only half of the $2^{N_f+1}$ qubit states are in the image, and hence an isometry rather than a unitary):\n"
msgstr "Kapag isinulat ang mapang ito para sa ilang estado, nagiging konkreto ang istruktura (tandaan na nakapirmi ang $b_0 = 0$, kaya kalahati lang ng $2^{N_f+1}$ na estado ng qubit ang nasa image, at kaya isang isometry ito sa halip na isang unitary):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single fermion on site 0 flips every cumulative parity above it, which is the delocalization at work. Collecting these columns into a matrix gives the isometry $W$, and the encoding is faithful when it *intertwines* the two Hamiltonians:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang fermion sa site 0 ay binabaligtad ang bawat cumulative parity sa itaas nito, na siyang delocalization na gumagana. Kapag tinipon ang mga column na ito sa isang matrix, makukuha ang isometry na $W$, at tapat ang encoding kapag *pinag-uugnay* nito ang dalawang Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{\\text{flow set}} \\, W = W \\, \\hat{H}_{\\text{JW}} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{\\text{flow set}} \\, W = W \\, \\hat{H}_{\\text{JW}} \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, mapping a fermionic state into the qubit space and then evolving it there must give the same result as evolving it in the fermionic space first and mapping afterward.\n"
msgstr "Ibig sabihin, ang pagmamapa ng isang fermionic na estado papunta sa espasyo ng qubit at pagkatapos ay pag-evolve rito doon ay dapat magbigay ng parehong resulta sa pag-evolve muna nito sa fermionic na espasyo at saka pagmamapa pagkatapos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The intertwining relation holds exactly, and separately for each flow set. That second, stronger statement is what later steps rely on: a product formula evolves the groups one at a time, and a product of intertwined factors is itself intertwined, so any *approximation* built from these groups agrees between the two encodings even though the encodings differ. As a corollary, the spectra must agree, with every Jordan-Wigner eigenvalue appearing twice in the larger space, once for each value of the unconstrained global parity:\n"
msgstr "Eksaktong totoo ang intertwining relation, at hiwalay para sa bawat flow set. Ang pangalawa at mas malakas na pahayag na iyon ang pinagbabatayan ng mga susunod na hakbang: ang product formula ay nag-e-evolve ng mga grupo nang isa-isa, at ang product ng mga intertwined na factor ay intertwined din, kaya anumang *approximation* na binuo mula sa mga grupong ito ay nagkakasundo sa pagitan ng dalawang encoding kahit magkaiba ang mga encoding. Bilang corollary, dapat magkasundo ang mga spectrum, kung saan ang bawat Jordan-Wigner eigenvalue ay lumilitaw nang dalawang beses sa mas malaking espasyo, minsan para sa bawat halaga ng walang-limitasyong global parity:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-fermionic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-build\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Build the fermionic circuit {#5-build-the-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "5. Buuin ang fermionic circuit {#5-build-the-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before involving any qubits, the dynamics are expressed on the *fermionic* level. A [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") acts on fermionic modes rather than qubits, and an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over the Hamiltonian is the whole circuit:\n"
msgstr "Bago gumamit ng anumang qubit, ipinapahayag ang dynamics sa *fermionic* na antas. Ang isang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ay umaandar sa mga fermionic mode sa halip na mga qubit, at ang isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") Gate sa ibabaw ng Hamiltonian ang buong circuit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A single Evolution gate spanning all four fermionic modes.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A single Evolution gate spanning all four fermionic modes.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is one opaque box over all four modes, and the interesting part is what it decomposes into. The `synthesis` argument says how: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") is the first-order product formula, which splits the operator by its [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") and evolves each group in turn. So the flow-set partitioning from step 2 *is* the Trotterization, and a single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) performs it, giving **one** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") **per flow set** in group order: east, west, then the diagonal interaction, carrying 3, 3, and 8 terms respectively.\n"
msgstr "Mayroong isang opaque na kahon sa lahat ng apat na mode, at ang kawili-wiling bahagi ay kung saan ito nade-decompose. Sinasabi ng argumentong `synthesis` kung paano: ang [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") ay ang first-order na product formula, na hinahati ang operator ayon sa mga [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") nito at ine-evolve ang bawat grupo nang paisa-isa. Kaya ang paghahati sa flow set mula sa hakbang 2 *ay* ang Trotterization, at isang [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) lang ang gumagawa nito, na nagbibigay ng **isang** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") **bawat flow set** ayon sa pagkakasunod ng grupo: east, west, tapos ang diagonal na interaksyon, na may dalang 3, 3, at 8 na term ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The same circuit decomposed into three Evolution gates, one per flow set.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The same circuit decomposed into three Evolution gates, one per flow set.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this happens entirely in fermionic space: no qubit has been mentioned yet, and the approximation is already made. The number of Trotter steps therefore belongs here too, as [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), which divides the time and repeats the whole sweep:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na lahat ng ito ay nangyayari sa fermionic na espasyo: wala pang nababanggit na qubit, at nagawa na ang approximation. Kaya ang bilang ng mga hakbang ng Trotter ay nabibilang din dito, bilang [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), na naghahati sa oras at inuulit ang buong sweep:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nine gates: the three flow sets, cycled through three times at a third of the time each. That cycling is what makes it a Trotterization rather than a re-slicing of one group. Repeating a *single* group would achieve nothing, since consecutive exponentials of the same operator commute, so `A(t/3) A(t/3) A(t/3)` is just `A(t)`. A formula that reads the groups can interleave them; one applied after the mapping cannot, because the grouping is gone by then.\n"
msgstr "Siyam na Gate: ang tatlong flow set, inuulit nang tatlong beses sa tig-isang katlo ng oras. Ang pag-ikot na iyon ang nagpapaging Trotterization nito sa halip na simpleng paghihiwa-hiwalay ng isang grupo. Ang pag-uulit ng *isang* grupo ay walang magagawa, dahil nagko-commute ang magkakasunod na exponential ng parehong operator, kaya ang `A(t/3) A(t/3) A(t/3)` ay `A(t)` lang. Ang formula na bumabasa sa mga grupo ay kayang pagsalitan ang mga ito; ang formula na ginamit pagkatapos ng mapping ay hindi, dahil wala na ang pagkakagrupo sa puntong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the step that makes the grouping matter. Each emitted gate is mapped and synthesized independently, so everything downstream acts on the partitioning decided at the fermionic level. Skipping the decomposition hands the whole operator to the next stage instead, and the grouping is ignored.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang hakbang na nagpapahalaga sa pagkakagrupo. Ang bawat inilabas na Gate ay minamapa at sini-synthesize nang hiwalay, kaya ang lahat ng susunod ay umaandar sa paghahating napagpasyahan sa fermionic na antas. Kapag nilaktawan ang decomposition, ibinibigay ang buong operator sa susunod na yugto at hindi na pinapansin ang pagkakagrupo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-with-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Transpile with the custom encoding {#6-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "6. I-transpile gamit ang custom na encoding {#6-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding is now ready to be used by the transpiler. Two more pieces are needed:\n"
msgstr "Handa na ngayong gamitin ng Transpiler ang encoding. Kailangan pa ng dalawang bahagi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A layout.** The default [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") assumes one qubit per mode, which is wrong in this situation. [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") associates the fermionic register with a [`QuantumRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.QuantumRegister) of a different size, which is how ancilla qubits enter the pipeline.\n"
msgstr "**Isang layout.** Ang default na [`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") ay nagpapalagay ng isang qubit bawat mode, na mali sa sitwasyong ito. Ang [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") ay iniuugnay ang fermionic register sa isang [`QuantumRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.QuantumRegister) na iba ang laki, na siyang paraan kung paano pumapasok ang mga ancilla qubit sa pipeline.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A synthesis plugin.** [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") takes the mapper function directly, maps the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate’s Hamiltonian with it, and emits a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), preserving the $e^{-itH}$ convention. Its [`product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\") decides how that gate is turned into rotations. Note that this is a *second*, independent product formula, acting on qubits after the mapping: Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) is passed here, and step 7 replaces it with one that knows about flow sets.\n"
msgstr "**Isang synthesis plugin.** Ang [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") ay direktang kumukuha ng mapper function, minamapa ang Hamiltonian ng [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") Gate gamit ito, at naglalabas ng [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), na pinapanatili ang convention na $e^{-itH}$. Ang [`product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\") nito ang nagpapasya kung paano gagawing mga rotation ang Gate na iyon. Tandaan na ito ay isang *pangalawa*, hiwalay na product formula, na umaandar sa mga qubit pagkatapos ng mapping: ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ng Qiskit ang ipinapasa rito, at papalitan ito ng hakbang 7 ng isang nakakaalam sa mga flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since every comparison below reruns this pipeline, it is worth wrapping once:\n"
msgstr "Dahil inuulit ng bawat paghahambing sa ibaba ang pipeline na ito, makabubuting ibalot ito nang isang beses:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four fermionic modes have become a five-qubit circuit, with the ancilla supplied by the custom layout.\n"
msgstr "Ang apat na fermionic mode ay naging isang circuit na may limang qubit, kung saan ang ancilla ay ibinigay ng custom na layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now look at what the resulting circuit actually contains. Decomposing repeatedly reduces the evolution gates all the way down to `U` and `CX`, so that the two-qubit cost of the two synthesis strategies compared below is measured in the same currency: [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#count_ops) then reports the `CX` count, and [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) takes a filter function to measure the two-qubit depth. Note that this `reps` is a decomposition depth, unrelated to the number of Trotter steps a product formula takes, which also goes by `reps` later in this guide:\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, tingnan natin kung ano talaga ang laman ng resultang circuit. Ang paulit-ulit na pag-decompose ay binabawasan ang mga evolution Gate hanggang `U` at `CX`, para ang gastos sa two-qubit ng dalawang synthesis strategy na pinaghahambing sa ibaba ay masukat sa parehong sukatan: ang [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#count_ops) ay mag-uulat ng bilang ng `CX`, at ang [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) ay kumukuha ng filter function para sukatin ang two-qubit depth. Tandaan na ang `reps` na ito ay isang depth ng decomposition, walang kaugnayan sa bilang ng mga hakbang ng Trotter na ginagawa ng isang product formula, na tinatawag ding `reps` sa mas huling bahagi ng gabay na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twenty-six `CX` gates in twenty-three layers, so almost nothing runs in parallel. Drawing the circuit shows why:\n"
msgstr "Dalawampu't anim na `CX` Gate sa dalawampu't tatlong layer, kaya halos walang tumatakbo nang sabay-sabay. Ipinapakita ng pagguhit ng circuit kung bakit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The transpiled circuit under LieTrotter's term-by-term synthesis, a long serial chain of CX ladders.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-16.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The transpiled circuit under LieTrotter's term-by-term synthesis, a long serial chain of CX ladders.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-16.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every term has been compiled in isolation: a basis change, a `CX` ladder down to a single rotation, then the ladder is undone. The weight-1 flow set is free; its terms are lone rotations with no ladder around them, but each weight-3 term pays for four `CX`gates, and because the ladders are emitted sequentially, nothing overlaps.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat term ay na-compile nang hiwalay: isang pagpapalit ng basis, isang `CX` ladder pababa sa isang rotation, tapos binabawi ang ladder. Libre ang weight-1 na flow set; ang mga term nito ay mga nag-iisang rotation na walang ladder sa paligid, pero ang bawat weight-3 na term ay nagbabayad ng apat na `CX` na Gate, at dahil sunud-sunod na inilalabas ang mga ladder, walang nagpapatong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the grouping survives the whole pipeline (three flow sets, three mapped [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)s) and still buys almost nothing. The fermionic Trotterization of step 5 did its job; what wastes it is the *qubit-side* formula. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) receives a set of terms it happens to be told nothing about, and compiles each in isolation. It cannot know they mutually commute, so it serializes what could share a basis change.\n"
msgstr "Kaya nananatili ang pagkakagrupo sa buong pipeline (tatlong flow set, tatlong na-map na [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)) pero halos walang naibibigay na pakinabang. Nagampanan ng fermionic Trotterization ng hakbang 5 ang trabaho nito; ang sumasayang dito ay ang formula sa panig ng *qubit*. Ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ay tumatanggap ng hanay ng mga term na wala itong alam tungkol sa istruktura, at kino-compile ang bawat isa nang hiwalay. Hindi nito alam na nagko-commute ang mga ito sa isa't isa, kaya sini-serialize nito ang maaari sanang magbahagi ng isang pagpapalit ng basis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the gap this encoding exists to close: two product formulas are at work, and only the fermionic one has been given the structure so far. The next step supplies a qubit-side synthesis that exploits it too.\n"
msgstr "Iyan ang puwang na nilalayong isara ng encoding na ito: dalawang product formula ang gumagana, at ang fermionic lang ang nabigyan ng istruktura hanggang ngayon. Ang susunod na hakbang ay nagbibigay ng synthesis sa panig ng qubit na sinasamantala rin ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"a-flow-set-aware-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. A flow-set-aware synthesis {#7-a-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"
msgstr "7. Isang synthesis na may alam sa flow set {#7-a-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recovering the advantage means telling the qubit-side synthesis about the structure. This is Section IV C of Ref. <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10): because all terms of a flow set commute, they can be simultaneously diagonalized by a single Clifford circuit, rotated in one shared basis and rotated back, instead of once per term.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagbawi sa bentahe ay nangangahulugang pagsasabi sa synthesis sa panig ng qubit tungkol sa istruktura. Ito ang Seksyon IV C ng Ref. <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10): dahil nagko-commute ang lahat ng term ng isang flow set, maaari silang sabay-sabay na i-diagonalize ng isang Clifford circuit, i-rotate sa isang pinagsasaluhang basis at i-rotate pabalik, sa halip na minsan bawat term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this encoding, the Clifford is simple. Conjugating by a chain of `CZ` gates on nearest neighbors maps\n"
msgstr "Para sa encoding na ito, simple ang Clifford. Ang pag-conjugate gamit ang isang chain ng mga `CZ` na Gate sa pinakamalapit na kapitbahay ay nagmamapa ng\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X_{j+1} \\; \\longmapsto \\; Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X_{j+1} \\; \\longmapsto \\; Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "simultaneously for every $j$. One `CZ` chain turns the entire weight-3 (west) flow set into a layer of independent single-qubit $X$ rotations. The [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) interface only requests a [`synthesize()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis#synthesize) method, which is all this class implements. It carries no number of Trotter steps, because it receives one flow set at a time and so cannot subdivide the evolution across the sets. That subdivision belongs a level up, in fermionic space, where an [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") sees all of them at once (see [step 9](#flowsets-check-dynamics)):\n"
msgstr "nang sabay-sabay para sa bawat $j$. Ang isang `CZ` chain ay ginagawang isang layer ng mga independent na single-qubit na $X$ rotation ang buong weight-3 (west) na flow set. Ang interface ng [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) ay humihingi lang ng isang method na [`synthesize()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis#synthesize), na siya lang ang ipinapatupad ng class na ito. Wala itong dalang bilang ng mga hakbang ng Trotter, dahil tumatanggap ito ng isang flow set sa bawat pagkakataon at kaya hindi nito mahahati ang evolution sa mga set. Ang paghahating iyon ay nabibilang sa mas mataas na antas, sa fermionic na espasyo, kung saan nakikita ng isang [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") ang lahat ng mga ito nang sabay (tingnan ang [hakbang 9](#flowsets-check-dynamics)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Two details are easy to miss. A custom [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) must expose a `preserve_order` attribute, which the high-level-synthesis pass reads.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Dalawang detalye ang madaling makaligtaan. Ang isang custom na [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) ay dapat maglantad ng attribute na `preserve_order`, na binabasa ng high-level-synthesis pass.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Both helpers emit their gates in explicit layers rather than in term order, because [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) schedules gates *as soon as possible, in the order they were added*. Since all the gates within one of these sets commute, the order is free to choose. A term-by-term synthesis chooses the order badly. Emitting the overlapping `CZ` chain sequentially reports a depth that grows with the qubit count rather than the constant `2` the hardware could achieve.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Parehong naglalabas ng kanilang mga Gate ang dalawang helper sa tahasang mga layer sa halip na ayon sa pagkakasunod ng term, dahil ini-schedule ng [`depth()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#depth) ang mga Gate *sa lalong madaling panahon, ayon sa pagkakasunod ng pagdaragdag*. Dahil nagko-commute ang lahat ng Gate sa loob ng isa sa mga set na ito, malaya ang pagpili ng pagkakasunod. Mali ang pagpili ng pagkakasunod ng synthesis na term-by-term. Ang sunud-sunod na paglalabas ng nagpapatong na `CZ` chain ay nag-uulat ng depth na lumalaki kasabay ng bilang ng qubit sa halip na ang pirming `2` na maaabot ng hardware.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Tandaan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is why the synthesis above carries no number of Trotter steps. It receives one flow set per gate, so a repetition inside it would repeat *within* a set rather than cycling between them:\n"
msgstr "  Ito ang dahilan kung bakit walang dalang bilang ng mga hakbang ng Trotter ang synthesis sa itaas. Tumatanggap ito ng isang flow set bawat Gate, kaya ang pag-uulit sa loob nito ay uulit *sa loob* ng isang set sa halip na umikot sa pagitan ng mga ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The first form buys nothing: consecutive exponentials of the same operator commute, so `A(t/2) A(t/2)` is just `A(t)` and the error stays at its one-step value however many steps are asked for.\n"
msgstr "  Walang naibibigay ang unang anyo: nagko-commute ang magkakasunod na exponential ng parehong operator, kaya ang `A(t/2) A(t/2)` ay `A(t)` lang at nananatili ang error sa halaga nito sa isang hakbang gaano man karaming hakbang ang hingin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The step count therefore belongs to the fermionic [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") of [step 5](#flowsets-build), which reads the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") and can interleave them. That division of labor is the point: the fermionic formula decides *how many steps* and *in what order*, and this class decides *how cheaply* each resulting set is realized.\n"
msgstr "  Kaya ang bilang ng hakbang ay nabibilang sa fermionic na [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") ng [hakbang 5](#flowsets-build), na bumabasa ng mga [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") at kayang pagsalitan ang mga ito. Iyan ang punto ng paghahati ng trabaho: ang fermionic na formula ang nagpapasya kung *ilang hakbang* at *sa anong pagkakasunod*, at ang class na ito ang nagpapasya kung *gaano kamura* ang pagsasakatuparan ng bawat resultang set.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To select the order, pass it to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\"), which is the argument `flow_set_pass_manager` takes. Nothing else about the pipeline (or the fermionic circuit it runs on) changes:\n"
msgstr "Upang piliin ang pagkakasunod, ipasa ito sa [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\"), na siyang argumentong kinukuha ng `flow_set_pass_manager`. Walang ibang nagbabago sa pipeline (o sa fermionic circuit na pinagtatakbuhan nito):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The flow-set-aware circuit, markedly shorter than the previous one, with entangling gates stacked into parallel layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-19.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The flow-set-aware circuit, markedly shorter than the previous one, with entangling gates stacked into parallel layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-19.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From depth 23 with 26 `CX` gates down to depth 12 with 22 `CX` gates. Note that this is fewer entangling gates and nearly half the depth. Comparing the two pictures, the difference is not that the gates are cheaper but that they *stack*. The serial ladders are gone; entangling gates now sit above one another in shared layers because the whole west flow set is rotated in a single shared basis and the interaction is emitted in layers of disjoint pairs.\n"
msgstr "Mula sa depth na 23 na may 26 na `CX` na Gate pababa sa depth na 12 na may 22 na `CX` na Gate. Tandaan na mas kaunti ito sa entangling na Gate at halos kalahati ng depth. Kapag ikinumpara ang dalawang larawan, ang pagkakaiba ay hindi na mas mura ang mga Gate kundi *nagpapatong-patong* ang mga ito. Wala na ang mga serial na ladder; ang mga entangling na Gate ay nakapatong na sa isa't isa sa mga pinagsasaluhang layer dahil ang buong west flow set ay iniikot sa isang pinagsasaluhang basis at ang interaksyon ay inilalabas sa mga layer ng magkakahiwalay na pares.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `FlowSetSynthesis` pattern-matches *absolute* qubit indices, which is safe here only because every flow set of this Hamiltonian spans the whole register. A fermionic product formula narrows each factor to the modes it actually touches, so a grouping whose sets covered only part of the chain would arrive relabeled and the patterns above would not match.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang `FlowSetSynthesis` ay nagpa-pattern-match sa *absolute* na mga index ng qubit, na ligtas dito dahil sumasaklaw sa buong register ang bawat flow set ng Hamiltonian na ito. Ang fermionic na product formula ay pinipikit ang bawat factor sa mga mode na talagang hinahawakan nito, kaya ang pagkakagrupong ang mga set ay sumasakop lang sa bahagi ng chain ay darating na may bagong label at hindi magtutugma ang mga pattern sa itaas.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both drawings show the circuit after `decompose(reps=6)`, which rewrites everything into the `U` and `CX` basis, so the `CZ`, `Rx`, and `Rzz` gates emitted by `FlowSetSynthesis` are not visible as such. That is deliberate: it puts both circuits in the same basis, which is the only way the two-qubit counts and depths above are comparable. It is the *layer structure* that is notable in these figures, not the gate labels.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ipinapakita ng dalawang drawing ang circuit pagkatapos ng `decompose(reps=6)`, na isinusulat muli ang lahat sa basis na `U` at `CX`, kaya ang mga Gate na `CZ`, `Rx`, at `Rzz` na inilabas ng `FlowSetSynthesis` ay hindi nakikita bilang ganoon. Sinadya iyon: inilalagay nito ang parehong circuit sa parehong basis, na siyang tanging paraan para maikumpara ang mga bilang at depth ng two-qubit sa itaas. Ang *istruktura ng layer* ang kapansin-pansin sa mga figure na ito, hindi ang mga label ng Gate.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"constant-depth-at-scale\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-scaling\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Constant depth at scale {#8-constant-depth-at-scale}"
msgstr "8. Pirming depth sa malaking sukat {#8-constant-depth-at-scale}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interesting question is not the count at four modes but how it *scales*. The two `CZ` brickwork layers do not grow with the chain length, so the two-qubit depth of one Trotter step should be constant. Measuring it directly on the full Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian, well past what could be simulated by brute force:\n"
msgstr "Ang kawili-wiling tanong ay hindi ang bilang sa apat na mode kundi kung paano ito *lumalaki*. Hindi lumalaki ang dalawang `CZ` brickwork layer kasabay ng haba ng chain, kaya dapat pirmi ang two-qubit depth ng isang hakbang ng Trotter. Direktang sinusukat ito sa buong Fermi-Hubbard Hamiltonian, malayo sa kayang i-simulate gamit ang brute force:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit **depth stays at 12** from four modes to 100, while [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) grows linearly to 407. The flow sets let it parallelize a little *within* the pipeline, but each set is still Trotterized term by term, so the growth is only slowed, not removed:\n"
msgstr "Ang two-qubit **depth ay nananatili sa 12** mula apat na mode hanggang 100, habang ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ay linear na lumalaki hanggang 407. Pinapayagan ng mga flow set na bahagyang mag-parallelize *sa loob* ng pipeline, pero ang bawat set ay Trotterized pa rin term-by-term, kaya pinabagal lang ang paglaki, hindi naalis:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two-qubit depth against number of modes; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 12.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-21.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two-qubit depth against number of modes; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 12.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/1d_fermi_hubbard-21.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gate count grows linearly under both (there are $O(N)$ terms to apply, and that is unavoidable), but the flow-set synthesis applies them in a constant number of parallel layers. This is the constant-depth result of Ref. <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10).\n"
msgstr "Linear na lumalaki ang bilang ng Gate sa dalawa (may $O(N)$ na term na kailangang ilapat, at hindi iyon maiiwasan), pero inilalapat ng flow-set synthesis ang mga ito sa pirming bilang ng mga parallel na layer. Ito ang constant-depth na resulta ng Ref. <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The depth 12 splits across the three flow sets as 0 + 4 + 8, at every chain length. The east flow set contributes **zero**; it is bare `Rx` rotations. The west flow set costs 4, from the two `CZ` brickwork layers going in and the two coming out; dropping the interaction leaves a two-qubit depth of **four** at any chain length. The remaining **eight** is the interaction whose `Rzz` terms act on both nearest and next-nearest neighbors and so need four disjoint layers, each costing two `CX`gates. Four is optimal here: every interior qubit carries four `Rzz` gates (two to each neighbor and two to each next-nearest one) and can only take part in one at a time, so no schedule can do better.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang depth na 12 ay nahahati sa tatlong flow set bilang 0 + 4 + 8, sa bawat haba ng chain. Ang east flow set ay nag-aambag ng **zero**; ito ay mga hubad na `Rx` rotation. Ang west flow set ay nagkakahalaga ng 4, mula sa dalawang `CZ` brickwork layer na papasok at dalawang palabas; kapag tinanggal ang interaksyon, ang natitirang two-qubit depth ay **apat** sa anumang haba ng chain. Ang natitirang **walo** ay ang interaksyon na ang mga `Rzz` na term ay umaandar sa parehong pinakamalapit at susunod-sa-pinakamalapit na kapitbahay kaya nangangailangan ng apat na magkakahiwalay na layer, na bawat isa ay nagkakahalaga ng dalawang `CX` na Gate. Pinakamainam ang apat dito: ang bawat panloob na qubit ay may apat na `Rzz` na Gate (dalawa sa bawat kapitbahay at dalawa sa bawat susunod-sa-pinakamalapit) at isa lang ang sabay nitong masasalihan, kaya walang schedule na makakagawa ng mas mahusay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Two thirds of the depth is the interaction, which shows that this encoding excels at the hopping, and thus at the dynamics of a free-fermion chain. However, note that the interaction does not commute with the hopping. Leaving it out is *not* an approximation to Fermi-Hubbard but a different model. Where the balance falls for a given problem is worth exploring.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dalawang katlo ng depth ay ang interaksyon, na nagpapakitang mahusay ang encoding na ito sa hopping, at kaya sa dynamics ng isang free-fermion chain. Gayunpaman, tandaan na hindi nagko-commute ang interaksyon sa hopping. Ang pag-alis dito ay *hindi* isang approximation sa Fermi-Hubbard kundi ibang modelo. Sulit tuklasin kung saan babagsak ang balanse para sa isang partikular na problema.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"check-the-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-check-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Check the dynamics {#9-check-the-dynamics}"
msgstr "9. Suriin ang dynamics {#9-check-the-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Under the domain-wall map, an occupation pattern becomes a cumulative-parity string, so the initial state is prepared differently than under Jordan-Wigner. This is an easily overlooked practical consequence of delocalizing the parity. The helper from step 4 gives the right label:\n"
msgstr "Sa ilalim ng domain-wall map, ang isang pattern ng occupation ay nagiging isang cumulative-parity string, kaya naiiba ang paghahanda ng paunang estado kumpara sa Jordan-Wigner. Ito ay isang praktikal na bunga na madaling makaligtaan ng delocalization ng parity. Ang helper mula sa hakbang 4 ang nagbibigay ng tamang label:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the state prepared, two questions remain, and they are best asked separately: does the flow-set synthesis compute the *right* thing, and does it compute it more *cheaply*?\n"
msgstr "Kapag handa na ang estado, dalawang tanong ang natitira, at pinakamainam na itanong ang mga ito nang magkahiwalay: kinakalkula ba ng flow-set synthesis ang *tamang* bagay, at kinakalkula ba ito nang mas *mura*?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Take correctness first. `FlowSetSynthesis` and Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) receive the same encoded flow sets from the same fermionic Trotterization, so they must realize the same unitary up to a global phase. The custom Cliffords reorganize the work; they do not change the result. Random statevectors detect any discrepancy far more cheaply than building the full unitary:\n"
msgstr "Unahin ang kawastuhan. Ang `FlowSetSynthesis` at ang [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) ng Qiskit ay tumatanggap ng parehong naka-encode na flow set mula sa parehong fermionic Trotterization, kaya dapat nilang isakatuparan ang parehong unitary hanggang sa isang global phase. Ang mga custom na Clifford ay nag-aayos muli ng trabaho; hindi nila binabago ang resulta. Natutukoy ng mga random na statevector ang anumang pagkakaiba nang mas mura kaysa sa pagbuo ng buong unitary:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both halves of that check matter. A unit-modulus overlap on a single state is necessary but not sufficient: a synthesis that got a state-dependent phase wrong would still show it. Requiring the *same* phase across several random states is what closes the gap. Checking more than one [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") matters too, since it confirms the agreement survives the interleaving of the flow sets rather than holding only for a single sweep.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Mahalaga ang dalawang kalahati ng pagsusuring iyon. Ang unit-modulus na overlap sa isang estado ay kailangan pero hindi sapat: ang synthesis na nagkamali sa phase na nakadepende sa estado ay lalabas pa rin. Ang pag-require ng *parehong* phase sa ilang random na estado ang nagsasara sa puwang. Mahalaga rin ang pagsusuri ng higit sa isang [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\"), dahil kinukumpirma nitong nananatili ang pagkakasundo sa pagsasalitan ng mga flow set sa halip na totoo lang para sa isang sweep.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the choice of qubit-side synthesis is free of consequence for accuracy, which is what makes a cost comparison meaningful. The remaining question is what the encoding as a whole buys against the obvious alternative: plain Jordan-Wigner on `num_sites` qubits, with no ancilla and no custom Cliffords. Both the encoding and the qubit-side synthesis differ between the two columns, but the check above showed the latter cannot affect the result, so what the fidelities test is the encoding. Both pipelines also start from the *same* fermionic Trotterization, so any difference in fidelity would indicate a bug rather than a trade-off. The two columns are the *encodings*, flow-set against Jordan-Wigner:\n"
msgstr "Kaya walang epekto sa katumpakan ang pagpili ng synthesis sa panig ng qubit, na siyang nagpapaging makabuluhan ng paghahambing ng gastos. Ang natitirang tanong ay kung ano ang naibibigay ng encoding sa kabuuan laban sa halatang alternatibo: payak na Jordan-Wigner sa `num_sites` na qubit, na walang ancilla at walang custom na Clifford. Parehong naiiba ang encoding at ang synthesis sa panig ng qubit sa pagitan ng dalawang column, pero ipinakita ng pagsusuri sa itaas na ang huli ay hindi makakaapekto sa resulta, kaya ang sinusubok ng mga fidelity ay ang encoding. Nagsisimula rin ang dalawang pipeline mula sa *parehong* fermionic Trotterization, kaya ang anumang pagkakaiba sa fidelity ay magpapahiwatig ng bug sa halip na isang trade-off. Ang dalawang column ay ang mga *encoding*, flow-set laban sa Jordan-Wigner:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the fidelity column first: identical, to every printed digit, in two different Hilbert spaces under two different encodings. That is the fermionic Trotterization showing through. The approximation was fixed in step 5, before either encoding was chosen, so both circuits carry exactly the error of a first-order formula over three flow sets, and it falls roughly four-fold per doubling of the step count.\n"
msgstr "Basahin muna ang column ng fidelity: magkapareho, sa bawat naka-print na digit, sa dalawang magkaibang Hilbert space sa ilalim ng dalawang magkaibang encoding. Iyon ang fermionic Trotterization na lumilitaw. Naayos ang approximation sa hakbang 5, bago napili ang alinmang encoding, kaya ang dalawang circuit ay may eksaktong error ng isang first-order na formula sa tatlong flow set, at bumababa ito nang humigit-kumulang apat na beses sa bawat pagdoble ng bilang ng hakbang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the encodings do differ in is cost, and the trade is worth stating plainly. The flow set spends **more** entangling gates: 22 against 18 at one step. The ancilla is not the reason, since it carries no two-qubit gate of its own. The reason is the interaction, exactly as [step 3](#flowsets-encoding) warned: delocalizing the parity turns three nearest-neighbor `ZZ` terms into seven spanning nearest *and* next-nearest neighbors, and each costs two `CX` gates. That is the price paid for making the hopping cheap.\n"
msgstr "Ang pinagkaiba ng mga encoding ay ang gastos, at sulit na sabihin nang tuwiran ang trade. Ang flow set ay gumagastos ng **mas marami** na entangling na Gate: 22 laban sa 18 sa isang hakbang. Hindi ang ancilla ang dahilan, dahil wala itong sariling two-qubit na Gate. Ang dahilan ay ang interaksyon, eksakto gaya ng babala ng [hakbang 3](#flowsets-encoding): ang pag-delocalize ng parity ay ginagawang pito ang tatlong nearest-neighbor na `ZZ` na term na sumasaklaw sa pinakamalapit *at* susunod-sa-pinakamalapit na kapitbahay, at bawat isa ay nagkakahalaga ng dalawang `CX` na Gate. Iyan ang presyong binabayaran para maging mura ang hopping.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It also wins only narrowly on depth at this size (12 against 14), because four modes is too small for the asymptotics to show. The point is the *scaling* measured in [step 8](#flowsets-scaling): that depth of 12 is constant, while the Jordan-Wigner depth grows with the chain. At 14 modes it is already 12 against 34.\n"
msgstr "Bahagya lang din itong nananalo sa depth sa laking ito (12 laban sa 14), dahil masyadong maliit ang apat na mode para lumitaw ang mga asymptotics. Ang punto ay ang *scaling* na sinukat sa [hakbang 8](#flowsets-scaling): pirmi ang depth na 12, habang lumalaki ang depth ng Jordan-Wigner kasabay ng chain. Sa 14 na mode, 12 laban sa 34 na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) calls above are essential, for two independent reasons.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Babala\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Mahalaga ang mga tawag sa [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) sa itaas, para sa dalawang magkahiwalay na dahilan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) and [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) use a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)’s *exact* definition, bypassing a custom qubit-side synthesis. Verifying against an un-decomposed circuit reports perfect fidelity even for a deliberately wrong synthesis.\n"
msgstr "  Ang [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) at [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) ay gumagamit ng *eksaktong* depinisyon ng isang [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), na nilalampasan ang custom na synthesis sa panig ng qubit. Ang pag-verify laban sa circuit na hindi dinecompose ay nag-uulat ng perpektong fidelity kahit para sa sadyang maling synthesis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The same applies one level up, to the fermionic synthesis. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate that is never decomposed goes to the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, which maps it without consulting `Evolution.synthesis` at all, so [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") would silently have no effect. `trotter_steps` from step 5 performs that decomposition; a pipeline that sets the method with [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") gets the same expansion from the pass instead.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ganoon din ang nalalapat sa isang antas pataas, sa fermionic synthesis. Ang isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") Gate na hindi kailanman dinecompose ay napupunta nang buo sa yugto ng fermion-to-qubit, na minamapa ito nang hindi sinasangguni ang `Evolution.synthesis`, kaya ang [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter.reps\") ay tahimik na walang magiging epekto. Ginagawa ng `trotter_steps` mula sa hakbang 5 ang decomposition na iyon; ang pipeline na nagtatakda ng method gamit ang [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") ay nakukuha ang parehong expansion mula sa pass.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a final cross-check, the site densities $\\langle n_j(t) \\rangle = (1 - \\langle V_j \\rangle)/2$ computed in the encoded space must reproduce the Jordan-Wigner result. This check is about the *encoding*, not the circuit, so no Trotter approximation enters it. Both time evolutions are computed exactly, by matrix exponentiation of the respective Hamiltonians. Any discrepancy would therefore point at the encoding rather than a product formula:\n"
msgstr "Bilang huling cross-check, ang mga densidad ng site na $\\langle n_j(t) \\rangle = (1 - \\langle V_j \\rangle)/2$ na kinalkula sa naka-encode na espasyo ay dapat magparami ng resulta ng Jordan-Wigner. Ang pagsusuring ito ay tungkol sa *encoding*, hindi sa circuit, kaya walang approximation ng Trotter na pumapasok dito. Parehong kinakalkula nang eksakto ang dalawang time evolution, sa pamamagitan ng matrix exponentiation ng kani-kanilang Hamiltonian. Kaya ang anumang pagkakaiba ay ituturo ang encoding sa halip na ang product formula:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The densities agree to ten decimal places.\n"
msgstr "Nagkakasundo ang mga densidad hanggang sampung decimal place.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Ang dapat tandaan {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Group before mapping.** Flow sets are defined on the directed fermionic interaction graph, so the grouping is chosen while problem structure is still available. The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") attribute carries it into the circuit, where a single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) turns it into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate per flow set.\n"
msgstr "**Mag-grupo bago mag-mapa.** Ang mga flow set ay tinutukoy sa directed na fermionic interaction graph, kaya pinipili ang pagkakagrupo habang available pa ang istruktura ng problema. Dinadala ito ng attribute na [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") papasok sa circuit, kung saan ginagawa ito ng isang [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) na isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") Gate bawat flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ancillas buy structure.** Spending one extra qubit turns an entire flow set into weight-1 Paulis, whose evolution needs no entangling gates. Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) observes this trade-off generally. Larger qubit-to-fermion ratios admit shallower evolution circuits.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mga ancilla ay bumibili ng istruktura.** Ang paggastos ng isang dagdag na qubit ay ginagawang weight-1 na mga Pauli ang buong flow set, na ang evolution ay hindi nangangailangan ng entangling na Gate. Ang Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10) ay naoobserbahan ang trade-off na ito sa pangkalahatan. Ang mas malalaking ratio ng qubit-sa-fermion ay nagpapahintulot ng mas mababaw na evolution circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A custom encoding is one function.** Map a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string; [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") do the rest.\n"
msgstr "**Ang custom na encoding ay isang function.** Imapa ang isang generalized na transfer operator sa isang Pauli string; ang [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") at [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") na ang bahala sa iba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The mapping and the grouping alone are not enough.** Splitting the evolution per flow set only slowed the linear growth in depth; a term-by-term synthesis of each set still threw away the fact that its terms commute. Only supplying a flow-set-aware [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) made the depth constant. Custom encodings, grouping, and custom synthesis are complementary: all three are needed.\n"
msgstr "**Hindi sapat ang mapping at pagkakagrupo lang.** Ang paghahati ng evolution bawat flow set ay nagpabagal lang sa linear na paglaki ng depth; ang term-by-term na synthesis ng bawat set ay sinayang pa rin ang katotohanang nagko-commute ang mga term nito. Ang pagbibigay lang ng [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) na may alam sa flow set ang nagpapirmi sa depth. Ang mga custom na encoding, pagkakagrupo, at custom na synthesis ay nagkukumplemento sa isa't isa: kailangan ang lahat ng tatlo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two product formulas, two jobs.** [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") fixes the approximation in fermionic space, where the grouping is still visible, so it alone sets the Trotter error and the step count. The qubit-side [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) then decides only how cheaply each set is realized: step 9 confirms both choices give the same unitary. Separating the two is what lets the accuracy and the cost be tuned independently. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"
msgstr "**Dalawang product formula, dalawang trabaho.** Ang [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") ang nag-aayos ng approximation sa fermionic na espasyo, kung saan nakikita pa ang pagkakagrupo, kaya ito lang ang nagtatakda ng Trotter error at bilang ng hakbang. Ang [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) sa panig ng qubit ay nagpapasya na lang kung gaano kamura ang pagsasakatuparan ng bawat set: kinukumpirma ng hakbang 9 na parehong unitary ang ibinibigay ng dalawang pagpili. Ang paghihiwalay ng dalawa ang nagpapahintulot na i-tune nang hiwalay ang katumpakan at ang gastos. Tingnan ang [Mag-synthesize ng Evolution gate sa fermionic na espasyo](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Verify it.** An encoding that satisfies the commutation relations might still represent a different Hamiltonian if a prefactor or sign is off. Checking an intertwining relation (or, more cheaply, the spectrum) catches this.\n"
msgstr "**I-verify ito.** Ang encoding na tumutupad sa mga commutation relation ay maaari pa ring kumatawan sa ibang Hamiltonian kung mali ang prefactor o sign. Nahuhuli ito ng pagsusuri sa isang intertwining relation (o, mas mura, ang spectrum).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `FlowSetSynthesis` above is deliberately written for *this* encoding on a 1D chain. It pattern-matches the specific Pauli labels the encoding produces and raises on anything else, rather than silently falling back to a generic product formula. A general implementation has two halves. Reading the flow-set structure from the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") is what a [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") for an evolution already does. Deriving the diagonalizing Clifford from the stabilizer group, as described in Section IV C of Ref.   <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), is the half that remains encoding specific.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang `FlowSetSynthesis` sa itaas ay sadyang isinulat para sa *encoding na ito* sa isang 1D chain. Nagpa-pattern-match ito sa mga partikular na label ng Pauli na nilalabas ng encoding at nagtataas ng error sa anumang iba pa, sa halip na tahimik na bumalik sa isang generic na product formula. Ang pangkalahatang implementasyon ay may dalawang kalahati. Ang pagbasa ng istruktura ng flow-set mula sa mga [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") ng operator ay ginagawa na ng isang [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\") para sa isang evolution. Ang pagkuha ng diagonalizing na Clifford mula sa stabilizer group, gaya ng inilarawan sa Seksyon IV C ng Ref.   <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id10), ang kalahating nananatiling partikular sa encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Also, delocalizing the parity makes the interaction term $n_j n_{j+1}$ weight-2 rather than diagonal in single qubits, which is the counterpart cost to the cheaper hopping terms.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Gayundin, ang pag-delocalize ng parity ay ginagawang weight-2 ang interaction term na $n_j n_{j+1}$ sa halip na diagonal sa mga single qubit, na siyang katumbas na gastos ng mas murang mga hopping term.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next: two dimensions {#next-two-dimensions}"
msgstr "Susunod: dalawang dimensyon {#next-two-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Everything above is one-dimensional, and deliberately so. On a chain, the flow sets are just the two arrow orientations, and the encoding needs a single ancilla. Neither simplification survives in two dimensions, which is where local encodings are needed.\n"
msgstr "Ang lahat sa itaas ay isang-dimensyon, at sinadya ito. Sa isang chain, ang mga flow set ay ang dalawang oryentasyon lang ng arrow, at ang encoding ay nangangailangan ng iisang ancilla. Wala sa dalawang pagpapasimpleng iyon ang nananatili sa dalawang dimensyon, kung saan kailangan ang mga lokal na encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On a planar lattice, a flow set is a directed path (or a union of vertex-disjoint directed paths) through the interaction graph, and finding a small set of such paths that covers every edge becomes a combinatorial problem in its own right, rather than a two-line classification. The encodings also change character; instead of a single ancilla for the whole chain, they add one per lattice site or cell. Verstraete-Cirac pairs every fermionic site with its own auxiliary qubit, a qubit-to-mode ratio of $2$, while Derby-Klassen places one at the center of each odd plaquette, for a ratio of $3/2$. The register layout then has genuine two-dimensional structure, and the stabilizer group that must be projected onto is no longer trivial. The encoded Hamiltonian is only faithful on a *subspace*, which changes both state preparation and the verification recipe from [step 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"
msgstr "Sa isang planar na lattice, ang flow set ay isang directed path (o unyon ng mga vertex-disjoint na directed path) sa interaction graph, at ang paghahanap ng maliit na hanay ng mga ganoong path na sumasaklaw sa bawat edge ay nagiging isang combinatorial na problema sa sarili nito, sa halip na isang dalawang-linyang klasipikasyon. Nagbabago rin ang katangian ng mga encoding; sa halip na iisang ancilla para sa buong chain, nagdaragdag sila ng isa bawat site o cell ng lattice. Ipinapares ng Verstraete-Cirac ang bawat fermionic na site sa sarili nitong auxiliary na qubit, isang ratio ng qubit-sa-mode na $2$, habang ang Derby-Klassen ay naglalagay ng isa sa gitna ng bawat odd na plaquette, para sa ratio na $3/2$. Ang layout ng register ay may tunay nang dalawang-dimensyong istruktura, at ang stabilizer group na dapat i-project ay hindi na trivial. Ang naka-encode na Hamiltonian ay tapat lang sa isang *subspace*, na nagbabago sa parehong paghahanda ng estado at sa recipe ng pag-verify mula sa [hakbang 4](#flowsets-verify).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pieces this guide builds are the ones that carry over: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") for a register whose size differs from the mode count, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") for the encoding itself, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") for wiring it into the transpiler, and a custom [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) for making the flow-set structure pay off. Only the encoding and the flow-set decomposition are different.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga bahaging binubuo ng gabay na ito ang dinadala pasulong: ang [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") para sa register na iba ang laki sa bilang ng mode, ang [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") para sa mismong encoding, ang [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") para ikabit ito sa Transpiler, at isang custom na [`EvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.EvolutionSynthesis) para pakinabangan ang istruktura ng flow-set. Ang encoding at ang flow-set decomposition lang ang magkaiba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [2D flow-set guide](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) picks up here, working through the Verstraete-Cirac encoding on a square lattice: four flow sets, a depth-2 Clifford for each, and the stabilizer projection the verification then needs.\n"
msgstr "Ipinagpapatuloy ito ng [2D flow-set guide](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard), na tinatalakay ang Verstraete-Cirac encoding sa isang square lattice: apat na flow set, isang depth-2 na Clifford para sa bawat isa, at ang stabilizer projection na kailangan ng pag-verify pagkatapos.\n"

